{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\fs22 What Is Wealth Management?\line \line Wealth Management is a holistic financial advisory and administration service designed to preserve, grow, protect, and transfer wealth across generations while managing risk, liquidity, tax exposure, and jurisdictional considerations.\line \line Unlike simple banking or investment services, wealth management integrates multiple financial disciplines into a single coordinated strategy, tailored to the clients net worth, asset complexity, legal structure, and long-term objectives.\line \line At its core, wealth management answers five fundamental questions:\line \line -\line How is wealth protected?\line \line -\line How is wealth grown?\line \line -\line How is wealth structured?\line \line -\line How is wealth accessed and deployed?\line \line -\line How is wealth preserved and transferred?\line \line What Wealth Management Is (In Practice)\line \line 1 Asset Preservation & Capital Protection\line \line Wealth management prioritizes preservation before growth.\line \line This includes:\line \line -\line Structuring assets to reduce exposure to litigation, seizure, or insolvency\line \line -\line Using trusts, foundations, and special purpose vehicles (SPVs)\line \line -\line Separating operating funds from protected or non-depleting capital\line \line -\line Jurisdictional diversification (multi-country custody and control)\line \line In private banking environments, this often includes:\line \line -\line Blocked funds structures\line \line -\line Non-depletion lending frameworks\line \line -\line Asset-backed credit rather than cash lending\line \line 2 Investment & Growth Strategy\line \line Wealth management is not speculative trading.\line \line It focuses on:\line \line -\line Risk-adjusted returns\line \line -\line Capital allocation across asset classes\line \line -\line Long-term yield and stability\line \line Typical asset classes include:\line \line -\line Public equities and bonds\line \line -\line Private equity and venture capital\line \line -\line Real estate and infrastructure\line \line -\line Commodities (gold, energy, agriculture)\line \line -\line Structured instruments (notes, guarantees, trade finance)\line \line -\line Digital assets and tokenized assets (where appropriate)\line \line The emphasis is on portfolio balance, not chasing yield.\line \line 3 Liquidity & Credit Optimization\line \line High-net-worth clients do not liquidate assets unnecessarily.\line \line Instead, wealth management:\line \line -\line Uses assets as collateral\line \line -\line Provides credit lines against portfolios\line \line -\line Enables liquidity without asset disposal\line \line -\line Separates ownership from usage\line \line Examples:\line \line -\line Lombard lending\line \line -\line Asset-backed credit facilities\line \line -\line SBLC/BG/MTN issuance backed by verified assets\line \line -\line Trade finance instruments supported by collateral structures\line \line This allows wealth to work twice: once as ownership, once as leverage.\line \line 4 Trust, Estate & Succession Planning\line \line A core function of wealth management is intergenerational continuity.\line \line This includes:\line \line -\line Estate planning\line \line -\line Trust formation and administration\line \line -\line Beneficiary structuring\line \line -\line Succession governance\line \line -\line Protection from probate, forced heirship, or political risk\line \line Proper wealth management ensures:\line \line -\line Wealth passes according to intent\line \line -\line Control is preserved\line \line -\line Family disputes are minimized\line \line -\line Assets remain productive after the principals lifetime\line \line 5 Tax & Jurisdictional Structuring\line \line Wealth management is tax-aware, not tax-evasive.\line \line It involves:\line \line -\line Choosing appropriate jurisdictions\line \line -\line Managing reporting obligations\line \line -\line Structuring income streams efficiently\line \line -\line Avoiding unnecessary tax leakage\line \line This is achieved through:\line \line -\line Trust jurisdiction selection\line \line -\line Holding company design\line \line -\line Treaty optimization\line \line -\line Asset location planning\line \line The objective is compliance with efficiency, not avoidance.\line \line 6 Governance, Reporting & Oversight\line \line Professional wealth management provides:\line \line -\line Consolidated reporting across all assets\line \line -\line Transparent performance tracking\line \line -\line Independent valuation\line \line -\line Risk oversight\line \line -\line Compliance and audit readiness\line \line This is essential for:\line \line -\line Institutional investors\line \line -\line Family offices\line \line -\line Trustees\line \line -\line Asset owners with complex portfolios\line \line What Wealth Management Is NOT\line \line To be very clear, wealth management is not:\line \line  Retail banking\line  Simple investment advice\line  Day trading or speculation\line  Product pushing\line  One-size-fits-all portfolios\line \line True wealth management is bespoke, structured, and relationship-driven.\line \line Who Wealth Management Is Designed For\line \line Wealth management is typically designed for:\line \line -\line High-net-worth individuals (HNWIs)\line \line -\line Ultra-high-net-worth families (UHNWIs)\line \line -\line Family offices\line \line -\line Trustees and fiduciaries\line \line -\line Asset holders with complex or illiquid wealth\line \line -\line Entrepreneurs with exit events\line \line -\line Institutions managing pooled or protected capital\line \line Wealth Management vs Private Banking\line \line Private Banking\line Wealth Management\line \line Transactional\line Strategic\line \line Account-focused\line Balance-sheet-focused\line \line Product-driven\line Structure-driven\line \line Short-term services\line Long-term stewardship\line \line In elite institutions, private banking is the delivery arm and wealth management is the brain.\line \line Why Wealth Management Matters\line \line Without proper wealth management:\line \line -\line Wealth erodes through taxes, inflation, and misallocation\line \line -\line Assets are exposed to unnecessary risk\line \line -\line Liquidity is mismanaged\line \line -\line Succession becomes chaotic\line \line -\line Wealth often disappears within 13 generations\line \line With proper wealth management:\line \line -\line Capital is protected\line \line -\line Growth is intentional\line \line -\line Credit is optimized\line \line -\line Legacy is preserved\line \line -\line Wealth becomes systemic, not fragile\line \line Thank you,\line US Capital Private Bank Client Relations}